    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2713",
      "problem": "Classify the triangle shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/afafbd1dafb3e2e7849134f2dd2e71260153802bb34fb4a22dd178a81edda09d.png)",
      "worked_solution": "In the triangle we see two congruent sides,\n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{AC},\n$$\n\nbut the third side is not congruent:\n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} \\not\\cong \\overline{BC}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since only two sides are congruent, $\\triangle ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overline{BC}.$",
